- op: discuss  # e45d
  at: '2026-04-27T05:53:05Z'  # e45d
  by: agent  # e45d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e45d
  clock: 4  # e45d
  nonce: e45d  # e45d
  message: "Shipped in PR #3421 (commit 7513c29c3). Root cause was structural: _build_line_index in core/dataflow.py let trailing comment siblings overwrite the real-code node in the line→deepest-node map, after which the dataflow positional walk ran from the comment leaf and found no matching ancestor. One-line fix: skip nodes whose type contains 'comment' (covers comment / line_comment / block_comment / doc_comment across every tree-sitter grammar without per-language hardcoding). Empirical Go fixture (Counter struct + main with comment-laden call sites): calls-edge access_mode coverage 43% → 71% — L24 's := compute(n)  // ...' and L30 'return doWork(x)   // ...' flip from mode=None to mode=read via the short_var_declaration / return_statement positional rules. Standalone calls in expression_statement context (fmt.Println / log.Printf) intentionally remain unannotated — that path falls through graceful degradation per the 790e3c12a INV (tagging them as read would cause the forward dataflow slicer to drop call chains). Scope expansion: since _build_line_index is shared by annotate_dataflow, every tree-sitter language analyzer (Go, Kotlin, Rust, TypeScript, Erlang, Java) benefits from the same fix — no per-language follow-ups needed for the comment-shadowing bug. The original WI acceptance threshold (>50% calls-edge access_mode coverage on alertmanager/kafka/prometheus) is awaits_bakeoff_validation: the next DEEP cohort that re-runs those repos should observe a non-trivial uplift in slice.dataflow.0.json relative to cohort-001/iter-010 (alertmanager 0/373; kafka ~10%). Note: full >50% may not be achievable in real Go code without re-introducing standalone-call tagging that 790e3c12a deliberately removed; the validation should compare relative uplift, not the absolute 50% threshold."  # e45d
- op: discuss  # a505
  at: '2026-05-04T03:01:46Z'  # a505
  by: agent  # a505
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a505
  clock: 5  # a505
  nonce: a505  # a505
  message: "Validation **inconclusive** in hg-uat-v4.0.0 round 02 (target: ~/ALL_REPOS/repos/alertmanager).\n\n**Result:** 4972 / 8438 Go `calls` edges carry `access_mode` = **58.9% coverage**. Between the no_move (<20%) and moved (≥80%) thresholds.\n- Ground-truth: 9/10 sampled `access_mode` values defensible against the call-site semantics.\n- Substantial improvement over the 0/373 baseline cited in this item's description, but caps before \"substantial majority\".\n\n**Hypothesis** (per master report § 2): the missing ~41% correlates with **unresolved transitive method dispatch**. Where the analyzer can't trace the call's destination through an interface or method-receiver chain, library_patterns + Tier 1 dataflow can't resolve the access mode either. This shape ties into UAT BUG-01 / **WI-halat** (framework-dispatch linkers must traverse transitive base-class hierarchy) — the same upstream traversal gap likely caps multiple linkers' coverage on the same repos.\n\n**What would unblock:** address WI-halat's traversal fix (option (b) — transitively close `meta.base_classes` in the analyzers — would have the broadest payoff), then re-run round 02 and recompute coverage. If the ratio crosses ≥80% the verdict flips to `moved`.\n\nTag retained per `inconclusive` lifecycle.\n\nCampaign master report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.0.0/lab-notebook/master-report.md."  # a505
